  "design_verdict": "REJECT",
  "explanation": "The engineer's calculation of the overturning moment from uplift is incorrect. The uplift distribution is triangular, with the maximum pressure at the heel and zero at the toe. The centroid of a triangle is located at one-third of the base distance from its tall side. In this case, the centroid of the uplift force is 1/3 of the base width (B/3) from the heel, which means its lever arm about the toe is 2/3 of the base width (2B/3). The engineer used B/3 (3.44 m) instead of 2B/3 (6.87 m) as the lever arm for the overturning moment calculation. Consequently, the overturning moment from uplift was halved, leading to an overstated Factor of Safety of 2.37. The corrected Factor of Safety is approximately 1.80 (17,942.4 / 9,944.8). While the corrected value still meets the acceptance criterion of 1.5, the calculation used to justify the design is incorrect and must be revised."
}

